# Java conventions

- Non-blocking only: Kafka/HTTP work via Vert.x `Future<T>`; no blocking calls on event loops
- Model types are Java 21 records under `model/`
- Config via `Env.resolve()` — env var → `-DNAME` → `-Dname.dotted` (env wins)
- Logging: SLF4J; package loggers follow existing `logback.xml` levels (`LOG_LEVEL_*` env vars)

## Testing

- Unit tests mirror package layout under `src/test/java/`
- Run `./gradlew test` before PRs; add tests for non-trivial metric or Kafka client behavior
- Do not add tests that only assert obvious behavior

## Kafka client notes

- AdminClient only; read-only DESCRIBE ACLs (cluster, topic `*`, group `*`)
- Request batching: `KAFKA_CHUNK_COUNT`, `KAFKA_CHUNK_DELAY_MS`
- Kafka 2.x: `MAX_TIMESTAMP` listOffsets unsupported — falls back to LATEST (expected WARN once per process)
